  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/assets/8b618c8e43dbe898a6e1c481f4f887a50bc2e8c658368876be11ec5ea269a50c.png)\n\nA company produces a chocolate bar that comes in an triangular-prism-shaped box. In the figure, the areas of some of the faces are displayed in a net of the prism. What is the total surface area of the box?",
  "worked_solution": "The surface area of our prism consists of $2$ triangles (base and top) and $3$ rectangles (central and side faces). \n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =2\\times (\\text{Area of the base})+2\\times (\\text{Area of the side faces}) \\\\  & +1\\times (\\text{Area of the central face}) \\\\  & =2\\times 36+2\\times 72+108 \\\\  & =72+144+108 \\\\  & =324\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
